+/**
+ * @file test_settings_advanced.cpp
+ * @brief Kiln OS: Settings > Advanced settings shows every row, or only the
+ *        everyday ones.
+ *
+ * Each page is built once with the setting on, then the setting is switched
+ * off and on again on the live page: the advanced rows hide and come back
+ * without a rebuild, and the everyday rows keep whatever their own bindings
+ * gave them. Every name is looked up, so a renamed row fails here instead of
+ * slipping out of the split.
+ */
